# Automation Studio

Read `skills/automation-studio/SKILL.md` in full first (gates G0–G7), then `references/n8n-building.md` before the first build.

Quick reference (`A="bash skills/automation-studio/scripts/auto.sh"`):
- `$A doctor` — if n8n isn't installed: `bash skills/automation-studio/scripts/setup_n8n.sh` (ask first), `--start` for the local server.
- Brief → plan JSON → `$A diagram plan.json -o out --formats png,html` → user sign-off.
- `$A new list` / `$A new <n> -o flow.ts` → `$A nodes …` / `$A node <type> --ts` → `$A build flow.ts -o flow.json` (validates).
- `$A test flow.json flow.cases.json` — all green before deploy. `$A creds flow.json` → user connects credentials.
- `$A deploy flow.json --target local [--activate]` (ask before activating) → `$A trigger` / `$A executions`.
- Other platforms: `$A convert flow.json --to node-red|make|zapier|power-automate|pipedream|activepieces -o out`.
- NEVER create accounts or type/print API keys — the user does it (references/credentials.md); keys live in ~/.config/ai-skills/automation-secrets.json.
